{"availability":"available","full":"VII-Cae/hyalite--liquid-glass","name":"hyalite--liquid-glass","description":"Real refraction liquid glass for the web: SDF lens maps + SVG displacement + backdrop-filter. One file, no WebGL.","category":"Design","language":"JavaScript","stars":234,"forks":12,"created":"2026-09-07T01:20:43Z","updated":"2026-09-11T12:58:50Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://vii-cae.github.io/hyalite--liquid-glass/demo/index.html","topics":["backdrop-filter","css","glassmorphism","liquid-glass","refraction","svg-filters"],"demo":"https://vii-cae.github.io/hyalite--liquid-glass/demo/index.html","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T13:02:06.193Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T13:02:06.193Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T13:02:06.193Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T04:29:41.876Z","stars":231,"forks":11},{"at":"2026-10-15T13:02:06.193Z","stars":234,"forks":12}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Real refraction “liquid glass” for the web. One file, no WebGL, no build step.","Hyalite treats an element as a slab of glass with a bevelled edge. For the element’s exact size and corner radii it computes a lens map, feeds it to an SVG filter, and lets the browser bend whatever is behind the element through backdrop-filter: url(#…). The centre stays clear; the edge pulls the world inward the way a thick piece of glass does, darkens where it magnifies, and catches a line of light along the rim. Straight lines curve, not smear.","Named after hyalite, the water-clear glassy opal. It also sounds like highlight, which is what the edge is about."],"features":["demo/index.html — all four engines at once, each on the settings its own release was shown at: 0.1.0 bends, 0.2.0 does it cheaply, 0.3.1 loses the staircase, 0.4.0 shades the edge and stops being shy about it, 0.5.0…","demo/edge-lab.html — the three bevel profiles side by side on one set of parameters, with an oscilloscope for the edge: displacement, the brightness the caustic implies, and the signed profile that comes out of them.","demo/cases.html — self-checking page: asymmetric, elliptical and overlap-rule radii, twins sharing a filter, size buckets, quarter-symmetry read back out of the map, a seam-free direction field on a circle, a dispersion…","demo/run-cases.mjs — not a page to open: a command-line script that runs cases.html in a real headless Chromium and prints red/green with an exit code. npm test, or node demo/run-cases.mjs (Node 22+, no dependencies).…"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/VII-Cae/hyalite--liquid-glass/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"db664c19edb19c7e1217e96ad23fb3bc47d651a3ec30833a1c2440a230153cf9","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T04:29:42.009Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T13:02:06.362Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Real refraction “liquid glass” for the web. One file, no WebGL, no build step.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/VII-Cae/hyalite--liquid-glass/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"db664c19edb19c7e1217e96ad23fb3bc47d651a3ec30833a1c2440a230153cf9","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/VII-Cae/hyalite--liquid-glass/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T13:02:06.362Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-09-11T12:58:50Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/VII-Cae/hyalite--liquid-glass/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T13:02:06.362Z","hash":"db664c19edb19c7e1217e96ad23fb3bc47d651a3ec30833a1c2440a230153cf9","originalBytes":21581,"storedBytes":21581,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["map","glass","one","edge","bevel","element","rim","filter","every","field","blur","back","displacement","radii","does","hyalite","light","backdrop","smooth","dispersion","pass","size","where","card","demo","frame","how","only","own","radius","side","slope","two","what","build","chromium","inside","over","which","after","along","centre","circle","corner","css","direction","each","ha